   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 594 of the laws of 2011, relating to authorizing the establishment of a long term care community in Columbia county known as Camphill Ghent, Inc. to provide integrated services to certain persons, in relation to statutory authorizations; and to repeal section 4 of such chapter relating thereto",
    "basePrintNo": "S6121",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6121-2011",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §§1 - 3, 5, rpld §4, Chap 594 of 2011",
    "lawSection": "Columbia County",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S6121\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act\nto amend chapter 594 of the laws of 2011, relating to authorizing the\nestablishment of a long term care community in Columbia county known as\nCamphill Ghent, Inc. to provide integrated services to certain persons,\nin\nrelation to statutory authorizations; and to repeal section 4 of such\nchapter relating thereto\n\nPURPOSE:\nThe purpose of this bill is to modify\nprovisions of Chapter\n594 of 2011 to allow residents of the adult home and assisted living\nprogram at Camphill Ghent to age in place.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nThis bill would provide necessary statutory\nexemptions that allows Camphill Ghent residents to \"age in place\" in\na fully integrated setting, subject to the approval of the\nCommissioner of Health and the Public Health and Health Planning\nCouncil, provided that there would be no rate adjustments or\nsupplemental payments to offset costs of additional services arising\nfrom such exemptions.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nCamphill Ghent is a continuous care facility for senior citizens\nlocated in Columbia County that serves individuals with developmental\ndisabilities along with other individuals in an integrated setting.\nIn an effort to address the needs for the aging population at\nCamphill Ghent, the Legislature passed Chapter 594 of the Laws of\n2011 that permits residents to remain at Camphill Ghent as they age and\nrequire more intensive care. This chapter amendment is necessary to\nclarify that the assisted living program at Camphill Ghent is subject\nto the approval of the Commissioner of Health and the Public Health\nand Health Planning Council. Further, this chapter amendment is\nnecessary to eliminate provisions requiring enhanced funding for\nCamphill Ghent as such funding is not currently accounted for in the\nState financial plan.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n\n",
